> ## Dual-mirror auto-sync (GitHub → HuggingFace)
> 
> `qmirror` is published to **two mirrors** that stay in sync automatically:
> 
> - canonical: <https://github.com/need-singularity/qmirror>
> - HF Hub:    <https://huggingface.co/need-singularity/qmirror>
> 
> A GitHub Actions workflow at [`.github/workflows/sync-to-hf.yml`](.github/workflows/sync-to-hf.yml)
> triggers on every push to `main` and uploads the working tree to HF via
> `huggingface_hub.upload_folder` (with `delete_patterns=["*"]` so deletions
> on GitHub propagate to HF). Wall lag is **~2-3 min** between push and HF
> visible commit.
> 
> **USER ACTION required to enable**: set the `HF_TOKEN` GitHub repository
> secret with a write-scope token at:
> 
> > <https://github.com/need-singularity/qmirror/settings/secrets/actions>
> 
> Until the secret is set, the workflow runs but **fails loudly** at the
> `Verify HF_TOKEN secret is present` step (printing the exact settings URL).
> This is by design — silent half-success is worse than a visible failure.
> 
> Local fallback for Actions-unavailable cases:
> [`tool/qmirror_pre_push_to_hf.hexa`](tool/qmirror_pre_push_to_hf.hexa)
> manually mirrors the tree using a locally-stored HF token.
> 
> Cost: $0 on the GitHub Actions free tier (public-repo unlimited minutes)
> + HF free tier (< 5 GB repo). Provenance:
> `anima/docs/qmirror_dual_mirror_autosync_landed_2026_05_03.ai.md`.
> 
